Maya: Heads-up — a user hit a mysterious failure when using the JS SDK inside a Next middleware (Vercel Edge): build failed with "Can't resolve 'fs'" and runtime lost trace headers.
Jon: that usually means a node-only import leaked into the bundle and our header handling mutated the incoming Headers. Which SDK version?
Maya: starter ships redwood-js-sdk@0.8.4. Stack points to token-cache and headers-merge.
Ivy: short fixes we should do: 1) stop using top-level node imports (move fs/undici imports into a node-only module and dynamic import them under an isNode guard); 2) add an explicit edge entrypoint and conditional exports so bundlers pick the lightweight adapter; 3) normalize/clone Headers defensively instead of mutating.
Jon: example minimal workaround users can try in middleware until we ship the fix: ```ts
import { createClient } from 'redwood-js-sdk/edge'
export async function middleware(req: Request) {
  const headers = Object.fromEntries(req.headers)
  const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY })
  await client.generate({ prompt: 'hi', headers })
  return new Response('ok')
}
```
Maya: thanks — that avoids both the build-time node import and the immutable Headers mutation. We'll add this to the starter docs.
Ivy: package.json exports sketch we plan to land: ```json
"exports": {
  "./edge": "./dist/edge.mjs",
  "./node": "./dist/node.cjs",
  "./": { "node": "./dist/node.cjs", "default": "./dist/edge.mjs" }
}
``` This gives an explicit edge subpath and a default that favors ESM/edge for bundlers.
Jon: TS note: split types into a DOM-friendly index.d.ts and node.d.ts for node-only shapes (Buffer, NodeJS.Timeout). Export subpath types so Next TS projects don't pull Node types.
Maya: I'll open a small PR: header normalizer + dynamic node imports + conditional exports + readme snippet. CI-bot: CI started for branch fix/edge-adapter-1832 — running next build fixture.
Docs-bot: Once CI is green we'll add a short "Edge middleware" section to the starter README with the snippet above and a migration note: avoid top-level client init in middleware (create inside handler).
Ivy: also add a tiny e2e that does a `vercel build` or `next build` on a middleware fixture to prevent regressions.
Maya: great, thanks. If anyone hits a similar build error, share the full build log and the path of the SDK import used (root vs /edge).
